nds, meeting RTO < 1 hour; ALB health checks and Auto Scaling replace unhealthy EC2 instances; minimum 2 instances across 2 AZs ensure the web tier survives a single AZ failure; 5-day backup retention enables point-in-time recovery meeting RPO ≤ 5 minutes; S3 cross-region replication can be added for photo disaster recovery.\n\nPerformance Efficiency: t3.micro instances are sized to deliver 40 rps per instance at 70% CPU utilization, matching capacity targets and avoiding under- or over-sizing; elastic Auto Scaling matches capacity to demand, scaling to 20 instances only during peak; CloudFront cache at 50% hit rate reduces origin load; ALB distributes requests evenly across instances; instance warm-up policies during scaling prevent request timeouts.\n\nCost Optimization: the design scales instances to match demand, minimizing idle capacity during 705 off-peak hours per month; CloudFront caching reduces redundant origin requests; t3.micro burstable instances offer lower cost than fixed-performance alternatives; no unnecessary premium services; storage and data transfer are sized exactly to requirements; monthly cost of $335.96 allows headroom within the $750 budget for future growth.",
